omx-clap-host (0.14.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * ci: test-fields runs in the job that has the toolchain and the CLAP
    headers, not in the contract job (#308)
  * ci: build against the published omx-contract v3.0.0 and plugin-hostd
    v0.7.0 (#308)
  * tests: the omx-delay plugin id is org.openmixer.delay, as omx-plugins
    0.13.0 ships it (#297)
  * 0.14.0 changelog: the hosting codes moved here, the six removed,
    omx-clap-scan --fields, contract.d/3 (K5, #297)
  * contract.d/3: the packages and CI install and expect omx-clap-core's
    files there, on omx-contract-devel >= 3.0.0 (K4, #297)
  * omx-clap-scan --fields: the field dump of one plugin, CLAP through the
    core's instance, LV2 through the adapter's world (K3, #297)
  * doc: omx-clap-scan --fields, the field dump plugin-hostd's tables read
    (K3, #297)
  * data/hosting: the six codes removed, featuresMissingAtLoad is
    featuresMissing; the render follows (K2, #297)
  * data/hosting in: the 16 hosting files of omx-contract, byte for byte;
    their render includes as omx_vocabulary.h did (K1, #297)
  * ci: the RPM file-lists check expects the udev rule omx-clap-host now ships
  * clap_scan_test runs every scanner from a scratch directory (#300)
  * docs: the idle hold bench says the watts per rate and path, the rest
    range as the rows have it, and names #298
  * jack e2e: the held arm reads the device's aggregate, not a literal 10
    (#296)
  * clap_unoffered_test compiles the idle hold in beside the core it includes
    (#296)
  * core test at ABI 16, and a VERSION move rebuilds the objects that embed
    it (#296)
  * docs: the CPU idle hold bench, every path at hold off, 10 and 0 with
    watts, jalv included (#296, #105)
  * jack e2e: a quit with a plugin active ends the hold too (#296)
  * bench: the jalv path's pids survive send's subshell, hostd counts its
    workers, and the jalv UI is opt-in (#296)
  * bench: the CPU idle hold as an arm, the device's answer and the window's
    watts beside each run (#296, #105)
  * bench: the tools build again under -Werror, the LV2 config's state_root
    given (#85)
  * packaging: the udev rule for cpu_dma_latency, in the RPM and the DEB
    (#296)
  * omx-clap-host: --idle-hold and the idle_hold command (#296)
  * Version 0.14.0: the idle hold adds to the ABI (#296)
  * core: libomx-clap-core holds cpu_dma_latency while an instance is active
    (#296)
  * contract: the idle hold's default and the hosting.idle dimension,
    declared in data/hosting.json (#296)
  * docs: the hosting comparison names its three follow-up issues (#267)
  * lv2 tests: the range arm's parameter infos start zeroed, for the
    compilers that cannot see they are read only once found (#254)
  * lv2: a control port that declares no bound gets -1e9 or 1e9 on that side,
    not [0,0] (#254)
  * lv2 parity: the three swh faults name their cause, the generator's lost
    activate reset (#230)
  * lv2: an llext:MidiPort is the only MIDI port its way, and its buffer
    keeps the stamp zynadd reads past the last event (#284)
  * lv2: the vendored rtmempool header names its licence (#265)
  * lv2: the vendored ll-plugins MIDI header names its licence (#284)
  * lv2: an llext:MidiPort is the MIDI port, over the ll-plugins LV2_MIDI
    buffer (#284)
  * review: the configuration-list rescan is reported while the plugin is
    inactive and dropped while active (#263)
  * cycle gate test: the dry-cycles count starts one cycle after the size is
    recorded (#289)
  * ci: the clean-root consumer runs core_link_test on the Makefile's fixture
    list, and the test resolves its paths (#288)
  * host: the host half of clap.audio-ports-config, its rescan the ports
    rescan the tick reports (#263)
  * docs: our LV2 adapter against mod-host and jalv, measured (#267)
  * review: the pool served under the header's spelling, the specification's
    and the deprecated URI; the maximum honoured; aligned chunks (#265)
  * fixture: the pool's two URIs declared lv2:Feature, so the validator knows
    them (#265)
  * lv2: the rtmempool feature, lv2dynparam's realtime-safe pool, under both
    its URIs (#265)
  * review: the warm-up reads the pass-through stage's width without a
    buffer, the ABI is 15, the scanner says the placement
  * docs: the desk hosts 433 of 433 CLAP plugins, nothing refused, every file
    scanned (#270)
  * docs: the desk hosts 429 of 429 CLAP plugins with the pass-through tools
    (#270)
  * tests: the layout checks take the ABI 15 words
  * host: a plugin with no audio port at all is a pass-through tool (#270)
  * review: a bundle failure is a reading, a trailing slash is stripped, the
    reader's contract is tested
  * abi: the baseline re-recorded at 0.13.0 with bundle_object in the 0.14
    node (#259)
  * ci: the consumer steps pass core_link_test its third fixture; a short
    invocation says so
  * docs: the desk measures 431 of 433 CLAP plugins hosted, every file
    scanned (#259)
  * map: bundle_object opens the node OMX_CLAP_CORE_0.14; 0.13 is frozen by
    the 0.13.0 release (#259)
